  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "In the academy Gu storage room, Fang Yuan ranks Black Boar Gu and White Boar Gu as the two highest value Gu in the Boar Gu series, above Jade Skin Gu and Liquor worm. A Black Boar Gu or a White Boar Gu sells for about six hundred primeval stones and is often bought as soon as it appears.",
        "chapters": [
          62
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "gu_black_boar_gu",
          "gu_white_boar_gu",
          "gu_jade_skin_gu",
          "gu_liquor_worm"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The text often names them together as Black and White Boar Gu when stating shared traits of that pair.",
        "chapters": [
          62
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Their ability is to change the Gu Master’s body constitution and raise strength permanently. The gain is small at a time but accumulates, belongs wholly to the Gu Master, and remains even if the Gu dies.",
        "chapters": [
          62
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "permanent-strength",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_master"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Black and White Boar Gu also give strength without needing primeval essence to keep that worth in play, and after one person has used them they can still be given to another.",
        "chapters": [
          96
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "permanent-strength",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Bai Ning Bing’s ice muscles, once achieved, are compared the same way: lasting strength like Black and White Boar Gu, with no primeval essence needed to sustain the remodel.",
        "chapters": [
          137
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "permanent-strength",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_bai_ning_bing"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Crocodile Strength Gu is classed with black and white boar Gu as a permanent strength raiser, precious and normally unavailable on the market.",
        "chapters": [
          204
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "comparisons",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_crocodile_strength_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In Shang clan city, Fang Yuan lists black and white boar Gu among the Gu he used to modify his body and raise strength. Wei Yang answers that they gave him the strength of two boars, and that such Gu permanently increase strength but are expensive investments.",
        "chapters": [
          280
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "comparisons",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_shang_clan_city",
          "char_wei_yang"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Brown bear innate strength Gu, black and white boar Gu, and crocodile strength Gu carry Great Dao law fragments of physical strength. That strength lurks in the body as beast phantoms until true power is unleashed.",
        "chapters": [
          292
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "comparisons",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_brown_bear_innate_strength_gu"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
